cond? Now I'm right now seeing&nbsp;&nbsp; Sneaker Dad: "I complain about them not standing&nbsp; up for anything. And when they do, I complain."&nbsp;&nbsp; What do they stand for? Yeah, name one thing that&nbsp; the Democrats have actually stood up for. I'm&nbsp;&nbsp; waiting.I told you, I've said in the past—I was&nbsp; a third-generation Democrat. And when they turned&nbsp;&nbsp; into the Republicans, I walked. Now they're worse&nbsp; than the Republicans. My mom took me door-to-door&nbsp;&nbsp; leafleting, pamphleteering for George McGovern&nbsp; in 1972. I worked for Democratic campaigns. I was&nbsp;&nbsp; youth coordinator for Dukakis in 1988. You know,&nbsp; I mean, I was as Democrat as they come. I was true&nbsp;&nbsp; blue. But I'm with you, John. They don't [ __ ]&nbsp; stand for anything. They're Republicans now. Yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp; they're Republicans—especially on these&nbsp; foreign-peace issues.If you say—wants to&nbsp;&nbsp; know—how much is the CIA involved in the color&nbsp; revolution in Mexico against the socialist&nbsp;&nbsp; president? I've received a couple of emails from&nbsp; friends in Mexico about this, and I would have to&nbsp;&nbsp; say that they probably are involved. Just because&nbsp; this thing lookstoo perfectly set up. I don't have&nbsp;&nbsp; any evidence on which to base that, but it looks&nbsp; like something's going on in Mexico. And there's&nbsp;&nbsp; also a question from—I just saw it—from...Well,&nbsp; there are two. One from Sean Whitman: "I've been&nbsp;&nbsp; watching you for a year. Love your insight. Thank&nbsp; you." A recent post by The Majority Report says&nbsp;&nbsp; Trump may have been an FBI informant. Do you&nbsp; think this is possible?Absolutely. Absolutely&nbsp;&nbsp; possible. Because listen—99.9 times out of a&nbsp; hundred, when the FBI goes to someone and says,&nbsp;&nbsp; "We're the FBI, we're doing an investigation,&nbsp; and we need your help," they're going to say,&nbsp;&nbsp; "Of course I'll help. I'